#. Tag: para
#: extending-quanta.docbook:29
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This chapter describes how to customize &quantaplus; to your particular "
"needs and how you can help &quantaplus; become better."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: extending-quanta.docbook:43
#, no-c-format
msgid "Document Type Editing Package (&DTEP;)"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: extending-quanta.docbook:45
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Document Type Editing Packages (&DTEP;s) are used in &quantaplus; to add "
"support for markup, scripting languages, and &CSS;. They allow &quantaplus; "
"to provide features like auto-completion and node trees. Their simplicity "
"and flexibility are what make &quantaplus; a fast, developer friendly &IDE; "
"for web developers. They are what make &quantaplus; an easy-to-use, "
"productive environment."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: extending-quanta.docbook:54
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&DTEP;s come in two flavors, Family 1, which are markups, and Family 2, "
"which are scripting and &CSS;. &DTEP;s are made up of two parts, the Tag "
"Folder and the Toolbars. Tag Folders are composed of two types of files, the "
"&descriptionrc; and TagXML files, which carry the extension .tag. Toolbars "
"are the handy, icon-oriented tabs of buttons (above the editing window) "
"which place text into a document faster than the user can type."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: extending-quanta.docbook:63
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&DTEP;s can be created manually (see below), <link linkend=\"download-"
"resources\">downloaded</link> or automatically created from an existing DTD. "
"See <xref linkend=\"converting-dtd\"/> for details about the conversion."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: extending-quanta.docbook:67
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This document describes how to make TagXML files, the &descriptionrc;, and "
"toolbars. In short, a &DTEP;."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: extending-quanta.docbook:72
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"TagXML files (.tag) define both the attributes specific to a tag and the "
"layout and contents of the properties dialog &quantaplus; shows for the tag. "
"The &descriptionrc; file provides rules and information on the &DTEP; "
"itself. Toolbars provide a quick means for adding tags into a document "
"without worry of mis-spellings and such."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: extending-quanta.docbook:81
#, no-c-format
msgid "Packaging"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: extending-quanta.docbook:83
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Tag Folders are just that, folders. They are composed only of the "
"&descriptionrc; and TagXML files. Tag Folders carry the name of the mark-up "
"language and version, if applicable. (For example, html-4.01-strict)"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: extending-quanta.docbook:91
#, no-c-format
msgid "TagXML"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: extending-quanta.docbook:93
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The table below lists the elements defined in TagXML and declares whether "
"they are required or not. While not all are required, it is recommended that "
"you use as many as you can so that other users can have a better experience "
"and more information to work with."
msgstr ""

