"dialog at the top of &quantaplus; and select <quote>Validate TagXML.</quote> "
"A dialog will present itself and you need only to follow the simple "
"directions."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: extending-quanta.docbook:911
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This feature is currently not present. Currently validation occurs when the "
"TagXML files are loaded into &quantaplus;."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: extending-quanta.docbook:919
#, no-c-format
msgid "TagXML Examples"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: extending-quanta.docbook:922
#, no-c-format
msgid "Family 1"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: extending-quanta.docbook:924
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The following will show you a valid Family 1 TagXML file. This file happens "
"to describe &W3C; &XML; Schema's &lt;schema> element. The file name for this "
"TagXML file would be schema.tag. Simple, eh?"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: literallayout
#: extending-quanta.docbook:931
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<markup>\n"
"&lt;?xml version=\"1.0\" encoding=\"UTF-8\"?>\n"
"&lt;!DOCTYPE TAGS>\n"
"&lt;TAGS>\n"
" &lt;tag name=\"schema\">\n"
"  &lt;label>\n"
"   &lt;text>id&lt;/text>\n"
"   &lt;location col=\"0\" row=\"0\"/>\n"
"  &lt;/label>\n"
"  &lt;attr name=\"id\" type=\"input\">\n"
"   &lt;tooltip>A unique ID for the element.&lt;/tooltip>\n"
"   &lt;whatsthis>A unique ID for the element.&lt;/whatsthis>\n"
"   &lt;location col=\"1\" row=\"0\"/>\n"
"  &lt;/attr>\n"
"\n"
"  &lt;label>\n"
"   &lt;text>version&lt;/text>\n"
"   &lt;location col=\"0\" row=\"1\"/>\n"
"  &lt;/label>\n"
"  &lt;attr name=\"version\" type=\"input\">\n"
"   &lt;tooltip>Version of the schema.&lt;/tooltip>\n"
"   &lt;whatsthis>Version of the schema.&lt;/whatsthis>\n"
"   &lt;location col=\"1\" row=\"1\"/>\n"
"  &lt;/attr>\n"
"\n"
"  &lt;label>\n"
"   &lt;text>targetNamespace&lt;/text>\n"
"   &lt;location col=\"0\" row=\"2\"/>\n"
"  &lt;/label>\n"
"  &lt;attr name=\"targetNamespace\" type=\"input\">\n"
"   &lt;tooltip>&URI; reference of the namespace of this schema.&lt;/"
"tooltip>\n"
"   &lt;whatsthis>&URI; reference of the namespace of this schema.&lt;/"
"whatsthis>\n"
"   &lt;location col=\"1\" row=\"2\"/>\n"
"  &lt;/attr>\n"
"\n"
"  &lt;label>\n"
"   &lt;text>xmlns&lt;/text>\n"
"   &lt;location col=\"0\" row=\"3\"/>\n"
"  &lt;/label>\n"
"  &lt;attr name=\"xmlns\" type=\"input\">\n"
"   &lt;tooltip>&URI; reference for one or more namespaces for use in this "
"schema.\n"
"   If no prefix is used, then components of that namespace may be used "
"unqualified.&lt;/tooltip>\n"
"   &lt;whatsthis>&URI; reference for one or more namespaces for use in this "
"schema.\n"
"   If no prefix is used, then components of that namespace may be used "
"unqualified.&lt;/whatsthis>\n"
"   &lt;location col=\"1\" row=\"3\"/>\n"
"  &lt;/attr>\n"
"\n"
"  &lt;label>\n"
"   &lt;text>attributeFormDefault&lt;/text>\n"
"   &lt;location col=\"0\" row=\"4\"/>\n"
"  &lt;/label>\n"
"  &lt;attr name=\"attributeFormDefault\" type=\"list\">\n"
"   &lt;items>\n"
"    &lt;item>qualified&lt;/item>\n"
"    &lt;item>unqualified&lt;/item>\n"
"   &lt;/items>\n"
"   &lt;tooltip>Default form for all attributes within this schema.&lt;/"
"tooltip>\n"
"   &lt;whatsthis>Default form for all attributes within this schema.&lt;/"
"whatsthis>\n"
"   &lt;location col=\"1\" row=\"4\"/>\n"
"  &lt;/attr>\n"
"\n"
"  &lt;label>\n"
"   &lt;text>elementFormDefault&lt;/text>\n"
"   &lt;location col=\"0\" row=\"5\"/>\n"
"  &lt;/label>\n"
"  &lt;attr name=\"elementFormDefault\" type=\"list\">\n"
"   &lt;items>\n"
"    &lt;item>qualified&lt;/item>\n"
"    &lt;item>unqualified&lt;/item>\n"
"   &lt;/items>\n"
"   &lt;tooltip>Default form for all elements within this schema.&lt;/"
"tooltip>\n"
"   &lt;whatsthis>Default form for all elements within this schema.&lt;/"
"whatsthis>\n"
"   &lt;location col=\"1\" row=\"5\"/>\n"
"  &lt;/attr>\n"
"\n"
"  &lt;label>\n"
"   &lt;text>blockDefault&lt;/text>\n"
"   &lt;location col=\"0\" row=\"6\"/>\n"
"  &lt;/label>\n"
"  &lt;attr name=\"blockDefault\" type=\"input\">\n"
"   &lt;location col=\"1\" row=\"6\"/>\n"
"  &lt;/attr>\n"
"\n"
"  &lt;label>\n"
"   &lt;text>finalDefault&lt;/text>\n"
"   &lt;location col=\"0\" row=\"7\"/>\n"
"  &lt;/label>\n"
"  &lt;attr name=\"finalDefault\" type=\"input\">\n"
"   &lt;location col=\"1\" row=\"7\"/>\n"
"  &lt;/attr>\n"
" &lt;/tag>\n"
"&lt;/TAGS>\n"
"</markup>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: extending-quanta.docbook:936
#, no-c-format
msgid "Family 2"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: extending-quanta.docbook:938
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The following will show you a valid Family 2 TagXML file. This file happens "
"to describe &PHP;'s overload function. The file name for this TagXML file "
"would be overload.tag."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: literallayout
#: extending-quanta.docbook:945
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<markup>\n"
"&lt;?xml version=\"1.0\" encoding=\"UTF-8\"?>\n"
"&lt;!DOCTYPE tags>\n"
"&lt;tags>\n"
"  &lt;tag name=\"overload\" type=\"function\" returnType=\"void\">\n"
"&lt;attr name=\"class_name\" type=\"string\" status=\"optional\"/>\n"
"  &lt;/tag>\n"
"&lt;/tags>\n"
"</markup>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: extending-quanta.docbook:952
#, no-c-format
msgid "&descriptionrc;"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: extending-quanta.docbook:954
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The &descriptionrc; file is, also, quite simple and there is an editor for "
"it accessible from <menuchoice><guimenu>DTD</guimenu><guimenuitem>Edit DTD "
"Settings</guimenuitem></menuchoice>. This will edit the &descriptionrc; for "
"a &DTEP; you can select from a list. In order to edit the &descriptionrc; "
"for a newly created &DTEP; you should create a simple &descriptionrc; with "
"the following entries:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: literallayout
#: extending-quanta.docbook:960
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<markup>\n"
"        [General]\n"
"        Version = Use 1 for &quantaplus; version &lt;=3.1.2 and 2 for any "
"version greater.\n"
"        Name = DTD definition string. (-//&W3C;//DTD HTML 4.01 Transitional//"
"EN)\n"
"        NickName = The beautified name of the DTD. (HTML 4.01 Transitional). "
"If not defined, Name is\n"
"        used as NickName.\n"
"      </markup>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: extending-quanta.docbook:963
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Once you have created it at put aside of the tag files, load the newly "
"created &DTEP; with <menuchoice><guimenu>DTD</guimenu><guimenuitem>Load DTD "
"Package (DTEP)</guimenuitem></menuchoice> and after it is loaded you can "
"proceed with editing the settings of the &DTEP;. Check the tooltips and the "
"whatsthis text of the entries in the editor dialog to understand the meaning "
"of each entry. Alternatively you can read the <filename>quanta/data/dtep/dtd-"
"description.txt</filename> from the source tarball containing a description "
"about the format."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: extending-quanta.docbook:969
#, no-c-format
msgid "User Defined Actions"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: extending-quanta.docbook:970
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Actions are very common in every application. You meed them often when you "
"use any application. Clicking on a toolbar icon, selecting a menu item or "
"using a shortcut usually executes an action. In &quantaplus; actions are "
"taken to the next level. Instead of hardcoded actions (that are created by "
"the application programmer at the source code level) it is possible for the "
"ordinary user to create and modify actions and by this way adding new "
"functionality to &quantaplus;. These are the user defined actions, and many "
"of the standard &quantaplus; actions are user defined (and user modifiable) "
"actions as well."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: extending-quanta.docbook:975
#, no-c-format
msgid "There are three types of user definable actions:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: link
#: extending-quanta.docbook:977
#, no-c-format
msgid "<link>Text actions</link>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: link
#: extending-quanta.docbook:978
#, no-c-format
msgid "<link>Tag actions</link>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: link
#: extending-quanta.docbook:979
#, no-c-format
msgid "<link>Script actions</link>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: extending-quanta.docbook:983
#, no-c-format
msgid "Creating actions"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: extending-quanta.docbook:984
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You can create an action by going to <menuchoice> <guimenu>Settings</"
"guimenu> <guimenuitem>Configure Actions</guimenuitem> </menuchoice> . Click "
"on <guibutton>New Action</guibutton> and you will face a similar dialog:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: extending-quanta.docbook:998
#, no-c-format
msgid "<guilabel>Type</guilabel>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: extending-quanta.docbook:999
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Specifies the action's type (<link linkend=\"text-actions\">Text</link>, "
"<link linkend=\"tag-actions\">Tag</link>, <link linkend=\"script-actions"
"\">Script</link>)."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: extending-quanta.docbook:1003
#, no-c-format
msgid "Text"
msgstr "Tèxt"

#. Tag: para
#: extending-quanta.docbook:1004
#, no-c-format
msgid "The user visible name of the action."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: term
#: extending-quanta.docbook:1008
#, no-c-format
msgid "The button near the <guilabel>Text</guilabel> label"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: extending-quanta.docbook:1009
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The icon assigned to this action. Click on it in order to change the current "
"icon."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: extending-quanta.docbook:1013
#, no-c-format
msgid "Tool tip"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: extending-quanta.docbook:1014
#, no-c-format
msgid "Short description of what the action does."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: extending-quanta.docbook:1018
#, no-c-format
msgid "Shortcut"
msgstr "Acorchi"

#. Tag: para
#: extending-quanta.docbook:1019
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The shortcut assigned to this action. Click on <guilabel>Custom</guilabel> "
"or the button near <guilabel>Custom</guilabel> to assign a shortcut; click "
"on <guilabel>None</guilabel> to remove the currently assigned shortcut."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: extending-quanta.docbook:1023
#, no-c-format
msgid "Container toolbars"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: extending-quanta.docbook:1024
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The user defined toolbars where this action appears. See <xref linkend="
"\"creating-toolbars-3-2\"/>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: extending-quanta.docbook:1028
#, no-c-format
msgid "Detailed Settings"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: extending-quanta.docbook:1029
#, no-c-format
msgid "Specific settings for the different type of actions. See below."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: extending-quanta.docbook:1036
#, no-c-format
msgid "<title>Text actions</title>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: extending-quanta.docbook:1040
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The simplest actions. You can enter some text in the <guilabel>Detailed "
"Settings</guilabel> area and whenever the action is executed this text will "
"be inserted in your document at the current cursor position. See the below "
"example."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: extending-quanta.docbook:1046
#, no-c-format
msgid "<title>Tag actions</title>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: extending-quanta.docbook:1047
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Useful to insert XML tags, but of course you can use them for other purposes "
"as well. <mediaobject><imageobject> <imagedata fileref=\"tag-actions.png\" "
"format=\"PNG\"/> </imageobject></mediaobject> <variablelist> <varlistentry> "
"<term><guilabel>&lt;tag&gt;</guilabel></term> <listitem><para>The name of "
"the tag.</para></listitem> </varlistentry> <varlistentry> "
"<term><guilabel>&lt;/tag&gt;</guilabel></term> <listitem><para>If checked "
"when the action is executed this text will be inserted as a closing tag. If "
"there is a selected area in the document before you execute the action, the "
"&lt;tag&gt; will be inserted before the selected area and the &lt;/tag&gt; "
"after.</para></listitem> </varlistentry> <varlistentry> <term><guilabel>Run "
"\"Edit tag\" dialog if available</guilabel></term> <listitem><para>If "
"checked and there is a tagXML file for this tag, a tag editing dialog will "
"be shown prior of inserting the tag inside the document, so you can fine-"
"tune the tag attributes.</para></listitem> </varlistentry> </variablelist> "
"The &lt;tag&gt; and &lt;/tag&gt; will be inserted as you've typed there. The "
"&lt;, &gt; or the / sign won't be automatically appended."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: extending-quanta.docbook:1070
#, no-c-format
msgid "<title>Script actions</title>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: extending-quanta.docbook:1074
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The most powerful action type. With the help of this action you can run "
"external applications (usually scripts, but it's not limited to scripts), "
"which can alter your document or use your document (or part of your "
"document) as input. Examples from &quantaplus; itself are the "
"<guibutton>Quick Start</guibutton> dialog, the various <guilabel>View In...</"
"guilabel> actions for the (X)HTML DTEPs."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: extending-quanta.docbook:1079
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"First you have to enter the name of your script with the interpreter as "
"well. Example: <command>sh /home/myHome/myScript.sh</command>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: extending-quanta.docbook:1083
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Although you can use full paths, the recommended way is to use the <command>%"
"scriptdir</command> variable in the command line, like <command>sh %"
"scriptdir/myScript.sh</command>. This way &quantaplus; will try to locate "
"your script in the following places: <itemizedlist> <listitem><para>global "
"script folder: <filename><envar>$KDEDIR</envar>/share/apps/quanta/scripts</"
"filename></para></listitem> <listitem><para>local script folder: "
"<filename><envar>$KDEHOME</envar>/share/apps/quanta/scripts</filename></"
"para></listitem> <listitem><para>your path: <envar>$PATH</envar></para></"
"listitem> </itemizedlist> There are other special variables that you can use "
"in the command line:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: extending-quanta.docbook:1092
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<command>%f</command>: will be replaced with the URL of the current "
"document. In case of local documents, file:/ will be stripped from the "
"document."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: extending-quanta.docbook:1093
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<command>%input</command>: will be replaced with the selected input. See "
"below."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: extending-quanta.docbook:1094
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<command>%projectbase</command>: will be replaced with the URL of the "
"current project. It is empty if no project is loaded."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: extending-quanta.docbook:1095
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<command>%pid</command>: will be replaced with the PID of the running "
"&quantaplus; process. If &quantaplus; is running in unique mode, the "
"\"unique \" text will be prepended to the PID number. Useful when you use "
"DCOP to control &quantaplus; from the external script."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: extending-quanta.docbook:1096
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<command>%userarguments</command>: useful in case of events. This entry will "
"be replaced by the event properties in the following order:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: term
#: extending-quanta.docbook:1098
#, no-c-format
msgid "First argument"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: extending-quanta.docbook:1099
#, no-c-format
msgid "The unique id of the script"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: term
#: extending-quanta.docbook:1102
#, no-c-format
msgid "Second argument"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: extending-quanta.docbook:1103
#, no-c-format
msgid "the event name"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: term
#: extending-quanta.docbook:1106
#, no-c-format
msgid "Third argument"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: extending-quanta.docbook:1107
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"the parameters for the event, usually the file name of the current document "
"or the path to the project file."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: extending-quanta.docbook:1113
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Aside of the above methods the script can receive input from &quantaplus; on "
"the standard input. In the <guilabel>Input</guilabel> combobox you can "
"select what to send to the standard input. Choices are:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: extending-quanta.docbook:1116
#, no-c-format
msgid "<guilabel>None</guilabel>: nothing is sent to the script."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: extending-quanta.docbook:1117
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<guilabel>Current document</guilabel>: the whole document is sent to the "
"script."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: extending-quanta.docbook:1118
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<guilabel>Selected text</guilabel>: the selected area of the document is "
"sent to the script. Using the <command>%input</command> variable usually "
"makes sense only when using this setting."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: extending-quanta.docbook:1121
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Similar to the <guilabel>Input</guilabel> you can catch the output of the "
"executed application. There are two kind of outputs: <itemizedlist> "
"<listitem><para>normal output, printed to the standard output;</para> </"
"listitem> <listitem><para>error messages, printed to the standard error.</"
"para> </listitem> </itemizedlist> You can specify what should happen with "
"the text printed to the standard output. This can be done by modifying the "
"value of the <guilabel>Output</guilabel> combobox:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: extending-quanta.docbook:1131
#, no-c-format
msgid "<guilabel>None</guilabel>: the output of the application is ignored."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: extending-quanta.docbook:1132
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<guilabel>Insert in cursor position</guilabel>: the output will be inserted "
"in the current document and the cursor position."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: extending-quanta.docbook:1133 extending-quanta.docbook:1134
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<guilabel>Replace selection</guilabel>: the selected area of the document "
"will be replaced with the output."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: extending-quanta.docbook:1135
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<guilabel>Create a new document</guilabel>: a new document will be created "
"and will contain all the output of the script."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: extending-quanta.docbook:1136
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<guilabel>Replace current document</guilabel>: the entire document will be "
"replaced with the output."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: extending-quanta.docbook:1137
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<guilabel>Message window</guilabel>: the output will appear in the "
"<guilabel>Messages</guilabel> toolview."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: extending-quanta.docbook:1140
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The choices for the standard error output (<guilabel>Error</guilabel>) are "
"the same as for the normal output."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: extending-quanta.docbook:1145
#, no-c-format
msgid "Creating Toolbars"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: extending-quanta.docbook:1147
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The following will show you how to create toolbars for a &DTEP;. Toolbars "
"are graphical elements that are assigned to actions. Actions, in "
"&quantaplus;, are the basis for nearly all the extensions that &quantaplus; "
"has and will acquire in the future. The same mechanism that defines an "
"action in &quantaplus; also enables auto-completion and tag dialogs. With "
"actions, the limit of what you can do is virtually limitless. For means of "
"an example, we will use <ulink url=\"http://tidy.sf.net\">&HTML; tidy</"
"ulink> on our web pages."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: extending-quanta.docbook:1159
#, no-c-format
msgid "From Scratch to Complete"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: extending-quanta.docbook:1161
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"To begin, you will need to create a user toolbar. Select <menuchoice> "
"<guimenu>Toolbars</guimenu> <guimenuitem>Add User Toolbar</guimenuitem> </"
"menuchoice>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: extending-quanta.docbook:1169
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If there are many tags for the markup language, it is recommended that you "
"split up the tags into logical groups. You will need to create a new user "
"toolbar for each group. In this case, there are not many, so we will be "
"making one toolbar and naming it with the name of the markup."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: extending-quanta.docbook:1176
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Once all your toolbars are created, you must add and configure the actions. "
"To do this, select <menuchoice> <guimenu>Settings</guimenu> "
"<guimenuitem>Configure Actions</guimenuitem> </menuchoice> <emphasis> </"
"emphasis>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: extending-quanta.docbook:1187
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The parts of this window are pretty straight forward. Press the "
"<guibutton>New action</guibutton> button at the bottom of the window to "
"enter the editing mode."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: extending-quanta.docbook:1193
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Fill in all of the necessary fields and add the tag to the appropriate "
"toolbar(s)."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: extending-quanta.docbook:1198
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Complete the rest and, if the tag has attributes and you always plan to use "
"them, check the <guilabel>Run \"Edit tag\" dialog if available </guilabel> "
"box so that you will be prompted every time the action is used."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: extending-quanta.docbook:1204
#, no-c-format
msgid "You should now have something much like the following."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: extending-quanta.docbook:1214
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Press the <guibutton>Apply</guibutton> button and you will see the action "
"added to the toolbar(s) you have selected."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: extending-quanta.docbook:1225
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Egad! That's an awful icon. How will yourself and others remember that icon "
"goes with that action? Let's replace it before trouble arises."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: extending-quanta.docbook:1230
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"To create an icon that more accurately describes that action, we will be "
"using &kiconedit;. Select it from the &kmenu;, <menuchoice> "
"<guisubmenu>Graphics</guisubmenu> <guisubmenu>More Programs</guisubmenu> </"
"menuchoice> (or where ever your distribution placed it)."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: extending-quanta.docbook:1238
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&kiconedit; defaults to the size 32x32 pixels, but we need 22x22. To change "
"this, select <menuchoice> <guimenu>Edit</guimenu> <guimenuitem>Resize</"
"guimenuitem> </menuchoice>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: extending-quanta.docbook:1247
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Keep in mind that you are creating an icon that will assist in helping not "
"only yourself to remember which action does what, but also other users of "
"the &DTEP;."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: extending-quanta.docbook:1253
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Since the tag I am creating the icon for is called <quote>start,</quote> I "
"have decided to create a <quote>Start sign.</quote> Using the color green "
"(green often interpreted as <quote>go,</quote> <quote>start,</quote> or "
"<quote>proceed</quote>) will, or, at least, should, convey a message to the "
"user that clicking this action will place the &lt;start&gt; tag in the "
"current document."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: extending-quanta.docbook:1268
#, no-c-format
msgid "Now that I am finished with the creation of the icon, I will save it."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: extending-quanta.docbook:1272
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Once you are done with creating the icon(s), you must associate the icon "
"with the action. To do this, open <menuchoice> <guimenu>Settings</guimenu> "
"<guimenuitem>Configure Actions</guimenuitem> </menuchoice> again (in "
"&quantaplus;) and select the action you made the icon for. Beside the "
"<guilabel>Text</guilabel> field, you will see a button, click it."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: extending-quanta.docbook:1283
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Select <guilabel>Other Icons</guilabel> and then click the <guibutton> "
"Browse</guibutton> button."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: extending-quanta.docbook:1288
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Goto the folder in which you saved the icon, select the icon, and click "
"<guibutton>OK</guibutton>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: extending-quanta.docbook:1293
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Press the <guibutton>Apply</guibutton> button and either continue to do the "
"same with the other tags, if any, or click <guibutton>OK</guibutton> to "
"finish."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: extending-quanta.docbook:1305
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Let us say you would like to add some common &quantaplus; functions to your "
"toolbar or maybe you think the toolbar would be better off organized in a "
"different manner with some separators to group the actions. Open the "
"<guilabel>Configure Toolbars</guilabel> dialog by going <menuchoice> "
"<guimenu>Settings</guimenu> <guimenuitem>Configure Toolbars</guimenuitem> </"
"menuchoice>. Make sure your toolbar is selected."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: extending-quanta.docbook:1316
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"I will be choosing the separator (top of the left column) for my toolbar. "
"Once you have selected the item you wish to add to your toolbar, press the "
"right arrow button. This will add it to your toolbar."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: extending-quanta.docbook:1328
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"I think I would like a quick way to access the <guilabel>Konqueror Preview</"
"guilabel>. I will select it and add it to the toolbar."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: extending-quanta.docbook:1339
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Note how the separator helps in grouping. Someone new to my toolbar might "
"have thought that the &konqueror; button was like or the opposite of the "
"start button."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: extending-quanta.docbook:1351
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Apply your changes and, when you are done, press <guibutton>OK</guibutton> "
"to finish."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: extending-quanta.docbook:1356
#, no-c-format
msgid "Ah, look at the fantastic new toolbar! Much more handy now."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: extending-quanta.docbook:1366
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Remember to test your toolbar, by clicking all the buttons, so that you know "
"the output is correct."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: extending-quanta.docbook:1377
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Now to save the toolbar, we will select <menuchoice> <guimenu>Toolbars</"
"guimenu> <guisubmenu>Save Toolbars</guisubmenu> <guimenuitem>Save as Local "
"Toolbar</guimenuitem> </menuchoice>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: extending-quanta.docbook:1386
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Save it to the correct folder. Since NeXML does not exist, I will just have "
"it to the top-level folder, but your toolbar(s) should be saved to the "
"correct folder. Make sure to adjust your &descriptionrc; to have it load "
"your toolbar(s) when a new file of that type is created."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: extending-quanta.docbook:1398 extending-quanta.docbook:1413
#, no-c-format
msgid "Creating Your Own Documentation"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: author
#: extending-quanta.docbook:1400
#, no-c-format
msgid "<firstname>Robert</firstname> <surname>Nickel</surname>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: email
#: extending-quanta.docbook:1404
#, no-c-format
msgid "robert@artnickel.com"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: extending-quanta.docbook:1415
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Probably the most notable additions to &quantaplus; for the general user "
"will be the addition of documentation for the markup or scripting language "
"that you like best. To that end, this chapter will explain how I create the "
"&PHP; documentation tree for my personal use."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: extending-quanta.docbook:1422
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Before starting on creating your own documentation, you may wish to check "
"out the <ulink url=\"http://quanta.sf.net/main1.php?contfile=resource\"> "
"&quantaplus; repository</ulink> to see if someone else has already done this "
"set."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: extending-quanta.docbook:1429
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"There are two parts to this process. First, you must obtain the existing "
"documentation for the markup/scripting/&etc; language that you are after. "
"Second, you have to create the <filename>docrc</filename> file. The first is "
"up to you, the second is what we will cover here."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: extending-quanta.docbook:1436
#, no-c-format
msgid "The general form of the docrc file is as follows:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: literallayout
#: extending-quanta.docbook:1441
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"#KDE Config File\n"
"[Tree]\n"
"Doc dir=<replaceable>path, relative to this file, of the documentation html "
"files</replaceable> &eg; php42/\n"
"#top level elements\n"
"Top Element=<replaceable>Your description for these documentation</"
"replaceable> &eg; &PHP; 4.2 documentation\n"
"\n"
"Section 1=Section1.html\n"
"Section 2=#Sec2.1,#Sec2.2,#Sec2.3\n"
"Sec2.1=Sec2.1.html\n"
"Sec2.2=Sec2.2.html\n"
"Sec2.3=Sec2.3.html\n"
"...\n"
"\n"
"[Context]\n"
"ContextList=func1,func2,tag1,tag2,tag3\n"
"func1=func1.html\n"
"func2=func2.html\n"
"tag1=tag1.html\n"
"tag2=tag2.html\n"
"tag3=tag3.html"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: extending-quanta.docbook:1444
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The <filename>docrc</filename> is broken down into two sections: Tree and "
"Context."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: extending-quanta.docbook:1449
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The Tree section defines the presentation aspect of the documentation in the "
"documentation tab. For example, you will see that in the &PHP; documentation "
"you have something akin to this:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: extending-quanta.docbook:1461
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Relating this to the above, my &PHP; <filename>docrc</filename> looks like "
"this:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: literallayout
#: extending-quanta.docbook:1467
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"#KDE Config File\n"
"\n"
"[Tree]\n"
"\n"
"Doc dir=php42/\n"
"\n"
"#top level elements\n"
"Top Element=PHP 4.2 documentation\n"
"\n"
"PHP 4.2 documentation=Table of Contents,#Getting Started,#Language "
"Reference\n"
"\n"
"Table of Contents=index.html\n"
"\n"
"Getting Started=Introduction, ...\n"
"Introduction=introduction.html\n"
"...\n"
"\n"
"Language Reference=Basic syntax, ...\n"
"Basic syntax=language.basic-syntax.html\n"
"..."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: extending-quanta.docbook:1470
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Notice the <literal>#</literal> in front of <quote>Getting Started</quote> "
"and <quote>Language Reference</quote>. This indicates that these are sub "
"containers in the tree and have content of their own. I do not believe that "
"there is a set limit to the depth here (other than that driven by sanity) "
"&mdash; use your judgment."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: extending-quanta.docbook:1478
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"For the Table of Contents, you will notice that it is referenced directly to "
"a file (and consequently shows up at the bottom of the tree view &mdash; "
"folders first!)."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: extending-quanta.docbook:1485
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Spaces do not adversely affect anything, but watch out for &amp; and &lt; "
"characters. These should likely be replaced by &amp;amp; and &amp;lt; "
"respectively in all of the &XML; based &quantaplus; resource files."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: extending-quanta.docbook:1492
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The Context section is the section of the docrc file that is used to "
"facilitate context sensitive help. For example, you are writing a &PHP; "
"script and you would like to see the documentation for the "
"<function>mysql_fetch_array</function> function. You simply highlight the "
"function and then press <keycombo action=\"simul\">&Ctrl;<keycap>H</keycap> "
"</keycombo> for context help. The documentation on "
"<function>mysql_fetch_array</function> will immediately display. There are "
"only two entry types here: the ContextList and the file association lines."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: term
#: extending-quanta.docbook:1505
#, no-c-format
msgid "ContextList"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: extending-quanta.docbook:1507
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Really simple, this is just a comma separated list of the context items you "
"wish to have available (for &PHP;, these are the functions for &PHP;)."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: term
#: extending-quanta.docbook:1514
#, no-c-format
msgid "File association lines"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: extending-quanta.docbook:1516
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"These are of the form context item=html doc page. &eg; acos=function.acos."
"html"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: extending-quanta.docbook:1524
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"A pared down version of my <filename>docrc</filename> Context section is as "
"follows:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: literallayout
#: extending-quanta.docbook:1530
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"#Keywords for context help\n"
"[Context]\n"
"ContextList=abs,acos,acosh,addcslashes,addslashes,...\n"
"\n"
"abs=function.abs.html\n"
"acos=function.acos.html\n"
"acosh=function.acosh.html\n"
"addcslashes=function.addcslashes.html\n"
"addslashes=function.addslashes.html\n"
"..."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: extending-quanta.docbook:1533
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Now you can just save your <filename>docrc</filename> file, save it in "
"<filename class=\"directory\">$<envar>HOME</envar>/.kde/share/apps/quanta/"
"doc</filename> or <filename class=\"directory\">$<envar>KDEDIR</envar>/share/"
"apps/quanta/doc</filename> for local or global use respectively. Then create "
"a folder (the one specified in your <filename>docrc</filename> file) in the "
"same folder as your <filename>docrc</filename> file and copy your &HTML; "
"pages in there."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: extending-quanta.docbook:1543
#, no-c-format
msgid "You will need to restart &quantaplus; to see your documentation."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: extending-quanta.docbook:1547
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Once you are sure that they are good and worth sharing, send the <filename> "
"docrc</filename> file along with a description of any pertinent information "
"on what documentation you used to the <ulink url=\"http://quanta.sf.net/"
"main1.php?contfile=resource\">&quantaplus; repository</ulink> for use by the "
"&quantaplus; community. You will not get rich, but you will feel great "
"knowing that you contributed to the best web development platform around."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: extending-quanta.docbook:1560
#, no-c-format
msgid "Sharing Resources"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: extending-quanta.docbook:1561
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"With &quantaplus; you are not alone. It is possible to share the various "
"resources (DTEP packages, toolbars with actions, scripts, templates) with "
"others. There are two ways to do it:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: term
#: extending-quanta.docbook:1565
#, no-c-format
msgid "Sending in Email"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: extending-quanta.docbook:1566
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The resources can be sent in email to your friends, partners or to whomever "
"you want. You will see the <guilabel>Send in Email</guilabel> menu entries "
"in various places, like <menuchoice><guimenu>DTD</guimenu><guimenuitem>Send "
"DTD Package (DTEP) in Email</guimenuitem></menuchoice>, "
"<menuchoice><guimenu>Toolbars</guimenu><guimenuitem>Send Toolbar in Email</"
"guimenuitem></menuchoice>, in the context menu of the files and folders in "
"the <guilabel>Templates</guilabel> and <guilabel>Scripts</guilabel> tree."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: term
#: extending-quanta.docbook:1570
#, no-c-format
msgid "Uploading to the main server"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: extending-quanta.docbook:1571
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The resources can be uploaded to our main repository, from where all other "
"&quantaplus; users can download them. The submissions are reviewed and made "
"available only if our team considers correct and useful will be published. "
"In order to make a valid submission it is suggested to sign the resources, "
"thus you need a GPG/PGP key. This information is used to verify the origin "
"of the resources both by our team and by the downloaders."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: extending-quanta.docbook:1572
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"About getting the resources from the main server see <xref linkend="
"\"download-resources\"/>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: extending-quanta.docbook:1573
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"When uploading you will be asked to enter the passphrase for your secret GPG "
"key (the passphrase will not be stored), or in the case of having more "
"secret keys, you will be able to pick up the one you want to use. In the "
"<guilabel>Share Hot New Stuff</guilabel> dialog fill the input fields (the "
"<guilabel>Preview URL</guilabel> may remain empty) and start the upload by "
"clicking <guilabel>OK</guilabel>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: extending-quanta.docbook:1574
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The upload can be initiated from <menuchoice><guimenu>DTD</"
"guimenu><guimenuitem>Upload DTD Package (DTEP)</guimenuitem></menuchoice>, "
"<menuchoice><guimenu>Toolbars</guimenu><guimenuitem>Upload Toolbar</"
"guimenuitem></menuchoice>, in the context menu of the files and folders in "
"the <guilabel>Templates</guilabel> and <guilabel>Scripts</guilabel> tree."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: extending-quanta.docbook:1583
#, no-c-format
msgid "Getting Resources"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: extending-quanta.docbook:1584
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"It is possible to upgrade your &quantaplus; without getting a new version, "
"by getting new resources like DTEP packages, toolbars with actions, "
"templates, scripts and documentation. One possibility is that you got the "
"resources in email or have downloaded from a web server, in which cases you "
"usually need to manually install them. In lucky case you also got an install "
"script when you have downloaded the resources. But &quantaplus; has a "
"dedicated server holding resources that were either not included in the main "
"distribution because of their sizes or infrequent usage, or they were "
"contributed later by users, and these resources are automatically installed. "
"Do download such resources use the various <guilabel>Download</guilabel> "
"menu entries. You can find them at <menuchoice><guimenu>DTD</"
"guimenu><guimenuitem>Download DTD Package (DTEP)</guimenuitem></menuchoice>, "
"<menuchoice><guimenu>Toolbars</guimenu><guimenuitem>Download Toolbar</"
"guimenuitem></menuchoice>, in the context menu of an empty area or toplevel "
"item in the <guilabel>Templates</guilabel>, <guilabel>Scripts</guilabel> and "
"<guilabel>Documentation</guilabel> trees."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: extending-quanta.docbook:1586
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"After a resource was downloaded, but before it is installed, &quantaplus; "
"verifies if the resource is valid, by checking the integrity and the "
"signature. In case of problems it warns you and you can decide if you want "
"to continue or not. Please read the warning dialogs carefully. In the case "
"when the integrity is correct and the resource is correctly signed, you will "
"still get an information dialog, so you can see who created the resource."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: extending-quanta.docbook:1590
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Be sure that you install resources, especially toolbars and scripts, only "
"from trusted sources!"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: extending-quanta.docbook:1595
#, no-c-format
msgid "Converting a DTD to a &DTEP;"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: extending-quanta.docbook:1596
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"It is possible to work on XML languages currently not supported by "
"&quantaplus; by creating a DTEP package. But the creation can be time "
"consuming, as you may need to write hundreds of tag files in <link linkend="
"\"tagxml-3-2\">tagXML</link> format. Of course, there is a nicer way to go, "
"by converting the DTD automatically into a DTEP package."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: extending-quanta.docbook:1598
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The conversion can be started from the <menuchoice><guimenu>DTD</"
"guimenu><guimenuitem>Load &amp; Convert DTD</guimenuitem></menuchoice> menu. "
"Select the <filename>.dtd</filename> file which defines the DTD you want to "
"use, and after that you will see the following dialog:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: extending-quanta.docbook:1605
#, no-c-format
msgid "The entries are:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: extending-quanta.docbook:1607
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<guilabel>Target directory name:</guilabel>the newly created &DTEP; will go "
"under this name to the <filename><envar>$KDEHOME</envar>/share/apps/quanta/"
"dtep</filename> folder."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: extending-quanta.docbook:1610
#, no-c-format
msgid "<guilabel>Name:</guilabel>the name (definition string) of the DTD"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: extending-quanta.docbook:1611
#, no-c-format
msgid "<guilabel>Nickname:</guilabel> the user visible name of the &DTEP;"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: extending-quanta.docbook:1612
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<guilabel>!DOCTYPE definition line:</guilabel> the string that should appear "
"in the !DOCTYPE tag, like HTML PUBLIC \"-//W3C//DTD HTML 4.01 Transitional//"
"EN\" \"http://www.w3.org/TR/html4/loose.dtd\""
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: extending-quanta.docbook:1615
#, no-c-format
msgid "<guilabel>DTD URL:</guilabel> the URL pointing to the DTD file"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: extending-quanta.docbook:1616
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<guilabel>Default extension:</guilabel> the extension usually used for files "
"that were written in this DTD"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: extending-quanta.docbook:1617
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<guilabel>Case-sensitive tags and attributes:</guilabel> self explaining, "
"usually true for XML language variants"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: extending-quanta.docbook:1618
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<guilabel>Fine-tune the DTEP after conversion:</guilabel> if checked, after "
"the conversion is done, &quantaplus; will bring up the &descriptionrc; "
"editor, so you can fine tune the newly created &DTEP;. It is recommended to "
"leave this options checked."
msgstr ""
